<title>UK: Allders investors vote down consolidation.</title>
<headline>Allders investors vote down consolidation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British department store and duty-free goods firm Allders Plc said on Thursday that its shareholders voted against plans for a share capital consolidation as recommended by the company.</p>
<p>On Wednesday it said it wanted to abandon the plans after a government clampdown on tax credits available on payouts.</p>
<p>Originally the group had planned a 50 million stg special dividend to accompany the consolidation. Instead Allders is proposing to pay a special dividend of 46 pence net per share as a second interim dividend, worth 50 million stg in total, subject to tax clearance. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
